00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,240
You don't need him to propose to you.

267
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,660
Maybe you could propose to him.

268
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,180
Oh, I don't know.

269
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:28,560
I don't know. Isn't that a little desperate?

270
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:30,120
I proposed to Chandler.

271
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:35,880
All right, moving on.

272
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,540
I don't think it was desperate.

273
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:39,640
It was amazing.

274
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:40,640
Thank you.

275
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:42,560
Well, do you think I should propose?

276
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:45,160
I think it could be kind of great.

277
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:46,060
Absolutely.

278
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,240
You'll love the feeling.

279
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,520
There's nothing like it.

280
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:54,380
Okay. Okay. So how should I do it?

281
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,740
How about at a game on the big screen?

282
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:59,500
How about at a Foot Locker?

283
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:03,900
What? What, he obviously thinks

284
00:15:03,900 --> 00:15:06,040
that's a nice way to be proposed to.

285
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:07,740
Plus, he'd never suspect it.

286
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:09,360
Yeah, that does make sense.

287
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,980
Okay, now, would you two like that?

288
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:13,140
Sounds good to me.

289
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:15,340
But what would a guy think?

290
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,280
- Nana's on the phone. - Wow.

291
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,060
That's interesting,

292
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:23,920
since she died seven years ago.

293
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:26,160
She did?

294
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,780
Who got her condo in Boca?

295
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:31,220
Hello?

296
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,780
It's our nanny.

297
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:35,700
Hi.

298
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:40,720
Oh, God, I hope you feel better. Okay. Bye.

299
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,980
That's Molly. She's sick.

300
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:44,600
Can you watch Emma today?

301
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:46,540
I can't. I have back-to-back classes.

302
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:48,140
Did Molly say what she had?

303
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:49,520
Because my throat's been hurting.

304
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:50,920
Menstrual cramps.

305
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:55,280
I don't think that's what this is.

306
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:58,420
Can any of you watch Emma?

307
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,920
No, I'm sorry, sweetie.

308
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:02,140
No, I've got work, and then I'm proposing.

309
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:05,360
Great. Shoot. What am I gonna do?

310
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:07,000
Well, I could do it.

311
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,780
Well, actually....

312
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,400
Can I talk to you for a second?

313
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:16,020
I do not want her babysitting our child.

314
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:16,840
Why not?

315
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,680
For one thing, she keeps calling her Ella.

316
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,800
Ella's a nice name.

317
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:23,240
Fine, we'll call the next one Ella.

318
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:24,560
- The next one? - Okay.

319
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:29,700
I don't want her watching our baby.

320
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:33,200
Ross, I am trying to help her become a better person.

321
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,020
This is a huge breakthrough for her.

322
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,720
She just offered to do something

323
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:38,440
for another human being.

324
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:41,100
You know, I don't know.

325
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:42,240
Ross, I'm telling you...

326
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:46,420
...she's giving up getting her eyebrows shaped to do this, all right?

327
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,660
Do you understand

328
00:16:47,660 --> 00:16:49,560
how important that is in our world?

329
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:54,380
Listen, I couldn't help but overhear,

330
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:56,180
because I was trying to.

331
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,240
Listen, let me do this.

332
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:01,240
I really want to help you guys out.

333
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:03,380
And plus, Rachel's been so wonderful to me.

334
00:17:06,884 --> 00:17:09,384
- Absolutely. - Oh, great!

335
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:10,940
So how much does it pay?

336
00:17:17,772 --> 00:17:18,960
Hi,Joe.

337
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:20,420
How's the second draft of the letter coming?

338
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:21,420
Great. I'm finished.

339
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,860
In fact, I just dropped it off at the agency.

340
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:27,640
- You dropped it off? - Yeah.

341
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:28,760
Can we read it?

342
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:30,200
Can you print out another copy?

343
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,640
No can do, <i>amigo.</i>

344
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:35,020
No, I didn't use the computer.

345
00:17:35,060 --> 00:17:36,860
It felt more personal to handwrite it.

346
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:40,900
- You handwrote it? - Yeah, and don't worry.

347
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:43,000
I didn't try to sound smart at all.

348
00:17:44,460 --> 00:17:44,980
See you later.

349
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,600
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

350
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:49,380
That letter is gonna go in our file.

351
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:51,280
We're never gonna get a kid.

352
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,540
We're gonna be one of those old couples...

353
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:56,520
...that collects orchids or has a lot of birds.

354
00:17:58,460 --> 00:17:59,420
It's okay. You know what?

355
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,520
I will just call the agency

356
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:03,420
and tell them to throw out the letter.

357
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:03,860
Okay, good.

358
00:18:05,580 --> 00:18:06,940
Hello, this is Chandler Bing.

359
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,260
Someone just dropped off

360
00:18:08,260 --> 00:18:10,620
a handwritten recommendation letter and....

361
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:17,480
Okay.

362
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,500
Thank you. Goodbye.

363
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,820
We're screwed, aren't we?

364
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:24,480
You know what?

365
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:25,980
Just tell me on the way to the bird store.

366
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:29,680
- They loved it. - What?

367
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:31,320
They thought it was very smart of us

368
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:33,580
to have a child write the letter.

369
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:37,080
They thought Joey was a child?

370
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:39,860
She guessed 8, 9, based on his drawings.

371
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:45,940
- Hi. - Hey, what'd you guys do today?

372
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,800
Ella wanted to go out,

373
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:50,760
so we went shopping and got some sushi.

374
00:18:51,860 --> 00:18:53,660
- That sounds like fun. - Yeah, not really.

375
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:55,900
Babies are dull.

376
00:18:58,438 --> 00:19:02,718
- Hey. Hi, how's my girl? - I'm fine.

377
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:05,460
And I got you a present

378
00:19:05,460 --> 00:19:07,080
for letting me stay with you.

379
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:09,040
- Ready? - Yeah.

380
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:15,540
You pierced her ears?

381
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,920
Doesn't it make her nose look smaller?

382
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:26,880
You pierced her ears?

383
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:29,000
How could you do this without telling me?

384
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,500
If I had told you,

385
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:32,340
then it wouldn't have been a surprise, now would it?

386
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,220
I think she looks cute.

387
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:37,200
But I am wrong.

388
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:41,860
Oh, my God. Oh, my God. Here comes Ross.

389
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:43,480
He's gonna flip out.

390
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:44,840
Why, did something happen

391
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:45,760
to his falafel cart?

392
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:48,520
- Hey, guys. - Ross!

393
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:50,220
Hi, Emma.

394
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:53,220
Why is she wearing her hat so low?

395
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:54,400
She can barely see.

396
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,780
I don't really want her to see.

397
00:19:58,340 --> 00:19:59,280
Why not?

398
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:02,320
Because there are so many terrible sights in this world.

399
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:05,580
Like war. Or that thing in Joey's refrigerator. Remember?

400
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:08,060
It was in a milk carton, but it looked like meat?

401
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:10,700
Come here.

402
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:14,780
There she is. Hi.

403
00:20:17,094 --> 00:20:19,534
- What? - Nothing.

404
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:22,000
Hi.

405
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:25,900
What--?

406
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:38,480
Please tell me those are clip-ons!

407
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:40,680
Oh, they're real.

408
00:20:41,660 --> 00:20:43,880
Did she do this to her?

409
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,060
I told you

410
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:46,680
we shouldn't have left Emma with her!

411
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:48,520
I know, I know. And you were right, Ross.

412
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:50,460
Okay? You are so irresponsible!

413
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:52,200
I am never letting you babysit again!

414
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:54,640
You know what? This kid needs me, okay?

415
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:57,080
She needs to have a cool, fun aunt.

416
00:20:57,140 --> 00:20:58,500
I'm a cool, fun aunt.

417
00:20:58,820 --> 00:20:59,260
Okay.

418
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:03,600
Hey! Monica can be cool and fun

419
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:05,360
at organized indoor projects.

420
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,320
All I wanted to do was help you

421
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,920
try to figure out what to do with your life.

422
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,420
This is how you repay me?

423
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:15,080
I don't need you to help me.

424
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:17,160
Because I already know what I'm gonna do with my life.

425
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:19,880
- Oh, yeah? Since when? - Since today.

426
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:25,880
I am going to be a baby stylist.

427
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:29,380
- What? - That's not a thing!

428
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:32,740
Well, it should be.

429
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:36,040
I'm gonna help babies learn how to accessorize...

430
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:37,900
...what colors to wear,

431
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:39,620
what clothes are slimming.

432
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:41,300
Babies don't care if they're slim!

433
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,720
Enter Amy.

434
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:46,660
Amy, l-- I just-- I just wanna--

435
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,260
What? What are you gonna do?

436
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:51,920
No more falafel for you!

437
00:22:04,430 --> 00:22:05,780
Great game, huh?

438
00:22:09,193 --> 00:22:10,683
Why do you keep looking at the screen?

439
00:22:10,781 --> 00:22:12,981
I'm not. I'm praying.

440
00:22:13,833 --> 00:22:15,813
Please let the Knicks win.

441
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:17,660
Thank you, Thor.

442
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:20,560
Where are you going?

443
00:22:21,460 --> 00:22:22,260
I'm going to the bathroom.

444
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:23,760
Well, I think you should wait.

445
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:24,680
Why?

446
00:22:26,280 --> 00:22:27,740
Well, if you don't hold it in,

447
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:29,440
you don't get all the nutrients.

448
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:33,560
<i>Knicks fans, please turn your attention</i>

449
00:22:33,760 --> 00:22:35,440
<i>to the big screen on the scoreboard.</i>

450
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:38,240
<i>Someone has a special question to ask.</i>

451
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:44,320
Mike Hannigan, will you marry me?

452
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:49,740
<i>Get a load of this.</i> <i>She's proposing to him!</i>

453
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,440
<i>Guess we know who wears</i> <i>the pants in that family.</i>

454
00:22:53,460 --> 00:22:55,080
Well, that's not very enlightened.

455
00:23:00,222 --> 00:23:02,602
Boo us? Boo you!

456
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:12,340
Hello? Yeah, this is Joey Tribbiani.

457
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:14,180
Oh, hi.

458
00:23:17,060 --> 00:23:18,520
Well, I'm glad you liked my letter.

459
00:23:20,980 --> 00:23:23,380
No, my mommy and daddy aren't home right now.

460
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:27,000
Okay, bye-bye.

461
00:23:31,155 --> 00:23:32,415
She was nice.

462
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:36,640
Joey, get Amy's bags. She is moving out.

463
00:23:38,860 --> 00:23:40,080
You're kicking me out?

464
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:42,880
You put holes in my baby's ears.

465
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:45,240
At least now people will know she's a girl!

466
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:50,680
I can't believe I ever even tried to help you.

467
00:23:50,740 --> 00:23:53,120
- You are so beyond help! - You know what?

468
00:23:53,380 --> 00:23:56,240
Ever since I got here, you have been nothing but negative.

469
00:23:56,500 --> 00:23:58,020
- Excuse me? - You didn't want me...

470
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:00,080
...to marry the old guy with the great apartment.

471
00:24:01,140 --> 00:24:05,920
Then I tried to help your daughter de-emphasize her flaws...

472
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:07,860
...and suddenly I'm the bad guy?

473
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,280
Joey, where are those bags?

474
00:24:09,300 --> 00:24:10,740
She has a lot of crap!

475
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:14,440
You know? When I moved in here,

476
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:16,200
I thought, "This will be so great.

477
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:19,360
Just us sisters back together again like when we were kids."

478
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:21,000
Except without that stupid Jill.

479
00:24:22,580 --> 00:24:24,740
Who has gotten fat, by the way.

480
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:27,640
Seriously?

481
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:30,880
Mom said she gained, like, 15 pounds.

482
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:32,700
- Hips or thighs? - Ass and face.

483
00:24:35,620 --> 00:24:38,200
Oh, my God! I thought she was on Atkins.

484
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:40,080
She was. Carbs found her.

485
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:47,320
See? This is what I wanted.

486
00:24:47,780 --> 00:24:50,140
Two sisters talking about real stuff.

487
00:24:53,820 --> 00:24:55,640
Oh, I can give you that.

488
00:24:56,420 --> 00:24:58,040
- You can? - Yeah.

489
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:01,720
I kept trying to make you a better person, but you're....

490
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:04,300
You're already a pretty perfect version of what you are.

491
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:07,000
Thank you.

492
00:25:08,100 --> 00:25:10,480
You gotta admit, Emma does look cute.

493
00:25:12,260 --> 00:25:13,760
Did you just say, "Emma"?

494
00:25:14,040 --> 00:25:15,400
Oh, I'm sorry. Ella.

495
00:25:22,460 --> 00:25:25,400
That woman didn't know what she was talking about, Mike.

496
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,960
Obviously, you have balls.

497
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:30,860
Please, let's forget the whole thing.

498
00:25:31,140 --> 00:25:32,160
I would love it.

499
00:25:32,340 --> 00:25:33,060
Consider it forgotten.

500
00:25:33,180 --> 00:25:33,640
Thank you.

501
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,540
But just so you know....

502
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:39,920
However and whenever you decide to propose,

503
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:41,520
I promise I'll say yes.

504
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:45,220
Whether, you know, it's at a basketball game...

505
00:25:45,220 --> 00:25:46,600
...or in skywriting...

506
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:50,140
...or, you know, like some lame guy in a cheesy movie...

507
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:51,360
...who hides it in the cake.

508
00:25:57,900 --> 00:25:59,720
It's in the cake, isn't it?

509
00:26:01,380 --> 00:26:04,320
Where else would lame Mr. No Balls hide it?

510
00:26:05,220 --> 00:26:06,660
What's the matter with me?

511
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:08,240
Why do I keep ruining this?

512
00:26:08,300 --> 00:26:09,300
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

513
00:26:09,300 --> 00:26:10,660
No, it's my fault.

514
00:26:10,660 --> 00:26:13,080
I keep trying to propose in these stupid ways...

515
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:15,180
...and I just wanna tell you I love you,

516
00:26:15,180 --> 00:26:17,200
and I wanna spend my life with you....

517
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:22,840
I'm gonna do this now.

518
00:26:23,780 --> 00:26:24,420
Oh, my God.

519
00:26:28,729 --> 00:26:29,559
Phoebe, l--

520
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:30,200
Wait. Oh, wait.

521
00:26:35,180 --> 00:26:36,340
Oh, no.

522
00:26:39,784 --> 00:26:40,924
Okay.

523
00:26:42,420 --> 00:26:43,200
Ready? Okay.

524
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:50,340
Phoebe, I love you.

525
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:53,060
There's no one else in the world

526
00:26:53,120 --> 00:26:55,380
I would ask to marry me three times.

527
00:26:58,020 --> 00:27:00,100
But I want to take care of you...

528
00:27:00,580 --> 00:27:02,640
...have babies with you...

529
00:27:03,440 --> 00:27:05,280
...and grow old with you.

530
00:27:07,580 --> 00:27:10,580
Phoebe Buffay, will you marry me?

531
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:12,220
Yes.

532
00:27:19,300 --> 00:27:22,080
- I love you. - I love you more.

533
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:23,460
Not possible.

534
00:27:33,227 --> 00:27:35,237
She's gonna be Mrs. No Balls!

535
00:27:41,981 --> 00:27:45,331
So how's the baby-styling business going?

536
